# MONOS — Dialog Content Flow (v1)

**Canonical cognitive model for every MonoStudio dialog.**

Visual chrome is frozen (`plan_dialog_tier_golden_reference_v1.mdc`). This rule governs **information hierarchy** — what the user reads, in what order.

---

## The flow

```
Hero
  ↓
Editable fields        ← INPUT     (what the user provides)
  ↓
Generated metadata     ← RESULT    (what the system derives)
  ↓
Information            ← EXPLAIN   (what will happen — not a duplicate of result)
  ↓
Footer                 ← ACTION    (confirm or cancel)
```

Mental model for the user:

1. **What do I enter?**
2. **What does the system produce?**
3. **What happens when I confirm?**
4. **Do I proceed?**

---

## Layer → components

| Layer | Role | Approved components |
|-------|------|---------------------|
| **Hero** | Context + title | `DialogHero` via `set_sidebar_brand` (L1) or `set_topbar_brand` (L2) |
| **Input** | User-editable | `FieldRow` + `PlainFieldInput`, `ComboField`, `DateField`, `PathField`, `WorkspacePicker`, … |
| **Result** | System-generated, read-only | `ProjectIdMetadataCard`, `MetadataCard` (value + mono footnote e.g. “Generated from…”) |
| **Explain** | Consequences, scope, side effects | `FieldRow` **hint** (when tied to an input) **or** `MetadataCard` **body** (standalone) |
| **Action** | Commit / dismiss | `GhostButton` Cancel + `GradientPrimaryButton` CTA (`add_footer_btn` / `add_footer_cta`) |

Use `add_form_stretch()` before **Result** so generated output sits in the lower “read” zone (see New Project).

---

## Reference mappings

### New Project (L1 — golden)

| Layer | Content |
|-------|---------|
| Hero | New Project · create in workspace |
| Input | Project name, Start date |
| Result | `PROJECT ID` card |
| Explain | Workspace picker + hint: *“All project data will be created in this workspace.”* |
| Action | Ghost Cancel · Gradient Create Project |

### Create Asset (L2)

| Layer | Content |
|-------|---------|
| Hero | Create Asset · add folder to project |
| Input | Type / Preset, Asset name |
| Result | `ASSET FOLDER` card (live from preset + name) |
| Explain | `MetadataCard` *On create* — work/publish subfolders from preset |
| Action | Ghost Cancel · Gradient Create Asset |

### Create Shot (L2)

| Layer | Content |
|-------|---------|
| Hero | Create Shot · add to sequence |
| Input | Sequence, Shot name |
| Result | `SHOT FOLDER` card |
| Explain | `MetadataCard` *On create* — department folders from shot preset |
| Action | Ghost Cancel · Gradient Create Shot |

---

## Anti-patterns

| Don't | Why |
|-------|-----|
| Repeat folder name in field hint **and** result card | Result layer already shows it |
| Use “Preset” card heading when Type / Preset field exists | Label duplication; use **On create** for explanation |
| Put explanation **before** generated result | Breaks Input → Result → Explain order |
| `InfoStrip` / new card chrome for explain | Use `MetadataCard` body or `FieldRow` hint |
| Skip Explain when side effects exist | User confirms blind |

---

## Checklist (new dialog)

- [ ] Hero names the flow in one line
- [ ] All user inputs are above `add_form_stretch()`
- [ ] Exactly one **Result** block per generated artifact (card language matches Project ID)
- [ ] **Explain** is unique — not repeated in hints, titles, or result footnotes
- [ ] Footer uses ghost + gradient CTA (L1/L2 create flows)
- [ ] Compared against New Project content order, not only pixels

---

## Future dialogs

Apply the same flow to **Import Asset**, **Publish**, **Settings** sections, etc.

Tier shell may differ; **content order must not.**
